{
  "slug": "artist:yung-lean",
  "name": "Yung Lean",
  "editorial_article": "Born in Stockholm in 1996, Swedish rapper Jonatan Aron Leandoer Håstad rose to international prominence in 2013 after his music video for 'Ginseng Strip 2002' became a viral phenomenon on YouTube. A central figure in the cloud rap movement, Lean co-founded the Sad Boys collective with producers Yung Gud and Yung Sherman, favoring a sound characterized by thick, melancholic atmospheres that helped define the SoundCloud rap era. In 2014, he released his debut studio album 'Unknown Memory' and embarked on a North American tour that included a performance at Webster Hall. Throughout his career, Lean has maintained a parallel project under the pseudonym Jonatan Leandoer96, exploring indie rock and neofolk on releases like 'Nectar' (2019). His work has earned industry recognition, including a 2019 Bram Stoker Medal for Cultural Achievement from Trinity College Dublin, and he has collaborated with artists such as Frank Ocean, Charli XCX, and Travis Scott.",
